{%- comment -%}
  Mobile-only dismissible review trust bar (WebwinkelKeur score).

  ROOT CAUSE FOUND (via direct DOM inspection): the earlier class name
  `sg-review-bar-on` — merely being added to <html>, regardless of any CSS
  matching it — was enough by itself to shrink the homepage slideshow's
  image to a tiny box. A generic, unrelated class name did NOT reproduce it.
  This store also has the Judge.me reviews app installed (a second reviews
  app alongside WebwinkelKeur, confirmed via its extension assets loading on
  every page) — almost certainly its own script watches for class changes
  containing "review" and misfires against unrelated elements. Renaming
  every class here away from the word "review" (now "trustbar") fixes it;
  verified directly in-browser that the slideshow image stays full-size with
  this class name where it collapsed with the old one.

  Two different, page-type-appropriate mechanisms push the header below it:
  - Homepage (`template-index`): the header overlays the hero via
    `position: absolute`. The bar floats `fixed` over everything, and ONLY
    the header's `top` is shifted to clear it.
  - Every other page (product, collection, etc.): the header is already in
    normal document flow there. The bar renders as an ordinary, non-fixed
    block — literally the first element in <body>, before the header — so
    normal CSS flow pushes the header (and everything after it) down.

  The x button hides it and remembers the choice (localStorage).

  Does NOT touch #wwkPreactRoot (the app's own floating badge). That badge
  already never renders on mobile (confirmed empty container there), and
  hiding it via CSS made the app's own script misbehave and break the page
  layout — so it's left alone entirely.

  To update the numbers, edit sg_review_score / sg_review_count below.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign sg_review_score = '9,5' -%}
{%- assign sg_review_count = '4' -%}

<script>
  (function () {
    try {
      var dismissed = localStorage.getItem('sgTrustBarDismissed') === '1';
      if (!dismissed && window.matchMedia('(max-width: 989px)').matches) {
        document.documentElement.classList.add('sg-trustbar-on');
      }
    } catch (e) {}
  })();
</script>

<div class="sg-trustbar" role="region" aria-label="Klantbeoordeling">
  <div class="sg-trustbar__inner">
    <span class="sg-trustbar__score">{{ sg_review_score }}</span>
    <span class="sg-trustbar__stars" aria-hidden="true">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</span>
    <span class="sg-trustbar__count">{{ sg_review_count }} Reviews</span>
    <span class="sg-trustbar__brand">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
      WebwinkelKeur
    </span>
  </div>
  <button type="button" class="sg-trustbar__close" aria-label="Sluiten">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18"/></svg>
  </button>
</div>

<style>
  .sg-trustbar { display: none; }

  @media (max-width: 989px) {
    :root { --sg-trustbar-h: 40px; }

    html.sg-trustbar-on .sg-trustbar {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 10px;
      width: 100%;
      height: var(--sg-trustbar-h);
      padding: 0 10px 0 12px;
      background: #e6007e;
      color: #ffffff;
      font-size: 13px;
      line-height: 1;
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    /* Homepage: float over everything; shift the header's `top` to clear it. */
    html.sg-trustbar-on body.template-index .sg-trustbar {
      position: fixed;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      z-index: 60;
      box-shadow: 0 1px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
    }

    html.sg-trustbar-on body.template-index .sg-header {
      top: var(--sg-trustbar-h) !important;
    }

    /* Every other page: normal in-flow block, first in <body> — ordinary
       document flow pushes the (already in-flow) header down naturally. */
    html.sg-trustbar-on body:not(.template-index) .sg-trustbar {
      position: static;
    }

    .sg-trustbar__inner {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      min-width: 0;
      overflow: hidden;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .sg-trustbar__score {
      flex: none;
      background: #ffffff;
      color: #e6007e;
      font-weight: 700;
      border-radius: 999px;
      padding: 3px 8px;
      font-size: 12px;
    }

    .sg-trustbar__stars {
      flex: none;
      color: #ffd21e;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
      font-size: 13px;
    }

    .sg-trustbar__count { flex: none; font-weight: 600; }

    .sg-trustbar__brand {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 4px;
      font-weight: 700;
      overflow: hidden;
      text-overflow: ellipsis;
    }

    .sg-trustbar__brand svg { flex: none; width: 14px; height: 14px; }

    .sg-trustbar__close {
      flex: none;
      width: 30px;
      height: 30px;
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      background: transparent;
      border: 0;
      color: #ffffff;
      cursor: pointer;
      padding: 0;
    }

    .sg-trustbar__close svg { width: 18px; height: 18px; }
  }

  /* Below the smallest phones, drop the brand label so the bar never wraps. */
  @media (max-width: 359px) {
    .sg-trustbar__brand { display: none; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  (function () {
    var bar = document.querySelector('.sg-trustbar');
    if (!bar) return;
    var closeBtn = bar.querySelector('.sg-trustbar__close');
    if (!closeBtn) return;
    closeBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
      document.documentElement.classList.remove('sg-trustbar-on');
      try { localStorage.setItem('sgTrustBarDismissed', '1'); } catch (e) {}
    });
  })();
</script>
